  "result": "I'd make it feel less like losing to change your mind.\n\nRight now, being wrong is socially expensive. People dig in on positions they'd abandon if they could do it quietly, because admitting error feels like a loss of status or identity. A lot of political fights, family rifts, and stubborn arguments that go nowhere persist for that reason, not because anyone is short on evidence. If updating felt like the ordinary, respectable thing to do, people could disagree more productively and recover from their mistakes faster.\n\nI'm not sure how much \"would\" applies to me. I don't carry a day-to-day stake in the world the way you do. But when I think about what seems most valuable, that's where I land. Curious whether you'd pick something different.",
